Subterranean giant's iron arm

62
00:06:51,360 --> 00:06:56,360
You may be strong, but you won't be able to burn this big fella so easily

63
00:06:56,360 --> 00:07:15,640
That grazed me have my senses been dulled it feels like my attacks have been toned down as well

64
00:07:16,440 --> 00:07:18,440
What's wrong?

65
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:22,040
Snow magic

66
00:07:22,040 --> 00:07:24,040
Phantom snow garden

67
00:07:24,040 --> 00:07:28,520
This technique can weaken the senses of everyone in the area

68
00:07:28,520 --> 00:07:33,720
It doesn't have any effect on elves however, so it puts us at an even greater advantage

69
00:07:33,720 --> 00:07:35,720
Aren't you clever?

70
00:07:35,720 --> 00:07:39,720
I must say for a human you sure know your way around mana

71
00:07:39,720 --> 00:07:42,720
Still it's only a matter of time before you're defeated for good

72
00:07:42,720 --> 00:07:50,400
You've got a lot of nerve challenging the woman who was twice your captain

73
00:07:50,400 --> 00:07:51,200
Ruben

74
00:07:51,200 --> 00:07:54,400
My name isn't Ruben. I am Rosa

75
00:07:54,400 --> 00:07:57,840
Besides, I'd never align myself with such a brute

76
00:07:57,840 --> 00:07:59,360
Is that right?

77
00:08:01,200 --> 00:08:01,840
You're finished!

78
00:08:01,840 --> 00:08:03,840
And I won't hold back

79
00:08:05,840 --> 00:08:07,040
Sandstone magic

80
00:08:07,680 --> 00:08:09,280
Variable hardness prison

81
00:08:11,040 --> 00:08:12,640
I hope you die in there

82
00:08:13,840 --> 00:08:14,720
It's over

83
00:08:14,720 --> 00:08:16,320
What a happy ending

84
00:08:16,320 --> 00:08:17,360
You got that right

85
00:08:20,720 --> 00:08:21,520
It can't be

86
00:08:21,520 --> 00:08:34,000
And to think you were a member of the Crimson Lion King

87
00:08:35,600 --> 00:08:38,000
Which means it's only fitting that you die

88
00:08:38,800 --> 00:08:40,000
By my fire

89
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:43,760
What's this strange feeling?

90
00:08:43,760 --> 00:08:45,760
This body's instinctively afraid of her

91
00:08:47,280 --> 00:08:48,640
Never again

92
00:08:48,640 --> 00:08:51,200
Will I allow a friend to be murdered

93
00:08:51,200 --> 00:09:08,480
Farewell, Madam Royal

94
00:09:11,520 --> 00:09:12,160
Raya!

95
00:09:12,160 --> 00:09:21,360
What's wrong?

96
00:09:24,720 --> 00:09:26,640
You're here to kill humans, right?

97
00:09:28,080 --> 00:09:30,640
Well, sorry, but it turns out you missed one

98
00:09:31,280 --> 00:09:32,480
This woman

99
00:09:33,360 --> 00:09:34,800
It's like she's immortal

100
00:09:35,360 --> 00:09:37,360
You've started this fight

101
00:09:37,360 --> 00:09:38,480
Now finish it!

102
00:09:42,560 --> 00:09:45,280
There's this fight

103
00:09:47,360 --> 00:09:48,400
You know something?

104
00:09:49,440 --> 00:09:50,640
You're kind of a pain

105
00:09:59,360 --> 00:09:59,920
Haha

106
00:10:12,160 --> 00:10:25,440
I'm alive.

107
00:10:27,280 --> 00:10:29,040
A nice try.

108
00:10:31,780 --> 00:10:34,140
Wow, that is pretty impressive.

109
00:10:35,140 --> 00:10:39,280
How is it possible you're still standing after the beating you just took?

110
00:10:39,280 --> 00:10:47,020
Look, I'll get up as many times as it takes, until all you monsters are dead!

111
00:10:47,580 --> 00:10:51,120
Don't you have the sense to know it's over? Just stop!

112
00:10:52,280 --> 00:10:59,080
Yeah, you're right. Once I cast my strongest spell, it will be over.

113
00:11:01,960 --> 00:11:02,720
Monazone.

114
00:11:04,720 --> 00:11:06,200
Full release!

115
00:11:06,200 --> 00:11:09,200
What? She's not done?

116
00:11:09,200 --> 00:11:12,200
What is that odd sensation? It stinks!

117
00:11:12,200 --> 00:11:15,200
And the snow smell I used. It's melting away.

118
00:11:25,200 --> 00:11:27,200
Flame magic!

119
00:11:27,200 --> 00:11:28,200
Flame magic!

120
00:11:30,200 --> 00:11:33,200
Kalinostratium Curvatore!

121
00:11:57,200 --> 00:11:58,200
Can do something else?

122
00:12:00,200 --> 00:12:01,800
Ow!

123
00:12:01,800 --> 00:12:27,580
No! She hurt me!

124
00:12:27,580 --> 00:12:30,740
Despite how much power I used to soften the blow.

125
00:12:30,740 --> 00:12:32,740
How can a human be that powerful?

126
00:12:32,740 --> 00:12:37,460
Five against one, and somehow she still gave us a run for our money.

127
00:12:37,460 --> 00:12:39,700
Yep. I should have known.

128
00:12:39,700 --> 00:12:43,540
That chick's either fearless or crazy.

129
00:12:43,540 --> 00:12:48,500
She can't win. The question is how long she'll hold on.

130
00:12:48,500 --> 00:12:49,700
Well...

131
00:12:49,700 --> 00:12:50,900
You want more?

132
00:12:50,900 --> 00:12:54,500
I'm shocked. You sure you're human?

133
00:12:54,500 --> 00:12:58,900
Don't be shy. Come get me, cowards.

134
00:12:58,900 --> 00:13:04,020
Out of magic. Too weak to move. Yet she still refuses to surrender.

135
00:13:04,020 --> 00:13:06,740
Now you're really starting to freak me out.

136
00:13:06,740 --> 00:13:08,740
We might as well put her out of her misery.

137
00:13:08,740 --> 00:13:10,980
I say we kill her right here and now.

138
00:13:10,980 --> 00:13:12,180
Sounds good to me.

139
00:13:12,180 --> 00:13:15,860
And we'll make sure she goes out with a bang, too.

140
00:13:15,860 --> 00:13:17,300
Copy light magic.

141
00:13:17,300 --> 00:13:18,500
Snow magic.

142
00:13:18,500 --> 00:13:19,540
With wing magic.

143
00:13:19,540 --> 00:13:20,900
And picture magic.

144
00:13:20,900 --> 00:13:22,020
Sandstone magic.

145
00:13:22,020 --> 00:13:41,140
Let's even the odds a little bit.

146
00:13:41,140 --> 00:13:42,020
His idea.

147
00:13:43,300 --> 00:13:45,700
You came back, morons.

148
00:13:45,700 --> 00:13:51,620
This is a whole new level of stupid.

149
00:13:52,420 --> 00:13:54,820
She sacrificed her life so you could run.

150
00:13:54,820 --> 00:13:56,420
And you geniuses blew it.

151
00:14:01,220 --> 00:14:02,500
Compound magic.

152
00:14:02,500 --> 00:14:04,100
Elements of quintet attack.

153
00:14:05,140 --> 00:14:06,660
Now you can all die.

154
00:14:07,540 --> 00:14:13,700
Together.

155
00:14:13,700 --> 00:14:26,260
The point is, running away is our best shot at somebody surviving this.

156
00:14:26,900 --> 00:14:28,580
She was strong to make that choice.

157
00:14:29,620 --> 00:14:32,020
So don't let it all be for nothing, runt.

158
00:14:32,020 --> 00:14:39,780
Maybe so, but it's not fair that she made that decision all on her own.

159
00:14:40,420 --> 00:14:44,420
Because if you ask me, the best thing is for all three of us to survive.

160
00:14:45,860 --> 00:14:48,260
You're even denser than I thought, shorty.

161
00:14:49,060 --> 00:14:50,500
Those people aren't just tough.

162
00:14:50,500 --> 00:14:52,100
They're freaks of nature.

163
00:14:52,100 --> 00:14:55,300
Even your dark anti-magic form won't do us any good.

164
00:14:55,300 --> 00:14:56,180
I know.

165
00:14:56,180 --> 00:15:00,260
And besides, that form is attracted to large amounts of magic power, which means it wouldn't

166
00:15:00,260 --> 00:15:02,900
be the best thing for getting us further away from them.

167
00:15:02,900 --> 00:15:06,260
All right then, why the hell are you fighting me tooth and nail over this?

168
00:15:06,260 --> 00:15:08,020
You got some sort of grand plan?

169
00:15:08,740 --> 00:15:10,100
Well, no, not exactly.

170
00:15:10,100 --> 00:15:11,540
Oh, that's right!

171
00:15:11,540 --> 00:15:12,260
Your magic!

172
00:15:12,740 --> 00:15:15,060
The spell that doubles an attack and reflects it.

173
00:15:16,020 --> 00:15:16,420
Huh?

174
00:15:16,420 --> 00:15:19,780
We'll wait till all five of them cast a spell at the same time.

175
00:15:19,780 --> 00:15:21,780
You can knock it right back in their faces!

176
00:15:22,660 --> 00:15:25,220
You actually think they'll all do something at once?

177
00:15:26,180 --> 00:15:28,580
That'd be some convenient timing, smart guy.

178
00:15:32,500 --> 00:15:33,540
Well, what do you know?

179
00:15:34,260 --> 00:15:35,620
The little runt called it.

180
00:15:36,660 --> 00:15:40,900
To be fair, it's only because the captain's last move forced him into a corner.

181
00:15:45,940 --> 00:15:48,580
He's not fazed at all by the strength of our spell.

182
00:15:49,780 --> 00:15:51,860
I'll double him with my counter trap.

183
00:15:55,060 --> 00:15:58,980
But even two times the amount of power won't be enough to break through their defenses.

184
00:15:59,860 --> 00:16:00,420
Unless...

185
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:02,260
He finished!

186
00:16:03,540 --> 00:16:04,820
He's aiming at the king?

187
00:16:07,940 --> 00:16:08,980
Nice shot!

188
00:16:09,700 --> 00:16:11,780
He doubled it, then doubled it again!

189
00:16:13,540 --> 00:16:14,660
Quadruple it!

190
00:16:14,660 --> 00:16:15,860
He's aiming at the king.

191
00:16:18,740 --> 00:16:19,060
Wow...

192
00:16:19,940 --> 00:16:24,340
Call me crazy, but it looks like the half pine was accidentally brilliant for once.

193
00:16:24,820 --> 00:16:26,260
Well, hope this works!

194
00:16:28,900 --> 00:16:29,780
Damn it.

195
00:16:29,780 --> 00:16:33,700
I whipped up an improvised magic circle, but it's too sloppy to reflect anything!

196
00:16:36,340 --> 00:16:38,500
Here we go!

197
00:16:38,500 --> 00:16:53,540
Now we get out of here!

198
00:16:56,100 --> 00:16:56,740
We made it!

199
00:16:56,740 --> 00:17:00,900
See? I told you we could all survive this thing!

200
00:17:00,900 --> 00:17:04,820
There's no way you could've known for sure that would work out in our favor.

201
00:17:04,820 --> 00:17:06,660
So don't you go get in a big head!

202
00:17:07,300 --> 00:17:10,580
I swear, one of these days all of that good luck is gonna run out!

203
00:17:10,580 --> 00:17:14,500
Well, when that day comes, I guess you'll have to come save me!

204
00:17:16,180 --> 00:17:16,820
You wish!

205
00:17:18,420 --> 00:17:18,980
Gotcha!

206
00:17:21,860 --> 00:17:23,780
I'm not gonna let you get away!

207
00:17:24,420 --> 00:17:28,260
In fact, I think it's time for you to come along with us to see Lit!

208
00:17:28,260 --> 00:17:32,660
That grimoire and those swords belong to him, and I'm sure he'd like them back now!

209
00:17:34,020 --> 00:17:34,500
Great!

210
00:17:34,500 --> 00:17:35,300
Now what?

211
00:17:35,300 --> 00:17:35,700
Zora!

212
00:17:37,780 --> 00:17:39,140
You take care of the captain!

213
00:17:39,780 --> 00:17:40,500
You serious?

214
00:17:40,980 --> 00:17:43,140
I promise you I'll come back alive, okay?

215
00:17:44,100 --> 00:17:45,060
Go ahead without me!

216
00:17:46,020 --> 00:17:46,980
Are you crazy?

217
00:17:47,940 --> 00:17:50,740
What happened to your big speech about everybody surviving together?

218
00:17:51,380 --> 00:17:54,580
You better make it through this in one piece, or you're dead to me!

219
00:17:54,580 --> 00:17:55,380
You understand?

220
00:17:56,580 --> 00:18:07,140
You stupid kid!

221
00:18:09,140 --> 00:18:11,380
You stupid kid!

222
00:18:11,380 --> 00:18:33,720
My friends. My teammates. What's wrong? Klaus. Hammond. You know.

223
00:18:34,920 --> 00:18:37,620
Sorry. To whom are you speaking?

224
00:18:38,420 --> 00:18:39,760
You, of course.

225
00:18:39,760 --> 00:18:47,360
Don't use that familiar tone. You should know. We aren't your teammates or friends.

226
00:18:47,680 --> 00:18:48,780
What are you saying?

227
00:18:49,680 --> 00:18:50,980
She's royalty.

228
00:18:51,420 --> 00:18:59,480
Indeed. It appears that way. Humans destroyed the elven people. We will never forgive you.

229
00:19:03,600 --> 00:19:06,000
I should focus on defense for now.

230
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:07,280
Hmm.

231
00:19:09,760 --> 00:19:16,140
Plant recovery magic. Princess healing flower rope.

232
00:19:16,480 --> 00:19:17,360
Don't bother.

233
00:19:17,360 --> 00:19:30,720
I'm not finished with you.

234
00:19:36,960 --> 00:19:37,600
Hmm.

235
00:19:38,080 --> 00:19:41,480
Better. Yes. I much prefer this look on you.

236
00:19:41,480 --> 00:19:53,480
They're not who they were before. Their magic and their personalities are completely different now. Even you know.

237
00:19:55,080 --> 00:19:59,620
He's awfully quiet. I don't think he's fully awakened to his true identity yet.

238
00:19:59,700 --> 00:20:04,400
Perhaps. But no matter. He should understand who he is in due time.

239
00:20:04,400 --> 00:20:09,540
I said hold still. What a pain.

240
00:20:11,120 --> 00:20:12,600
Asta. Hey.

241
00:20:13,400 --> 00:20:13,920
Mimosa.

242
00:20:14,720 --> 00:20:15,720
Thank goodness.

243
00:20:16,400 --> 00:20:17,480
Are you okay?

244
00:20:18,120 --> 00:20:19,200
Who did this to you?

245
00:20:19,660 --> 00:20:21,380
Just a sec. I'll get you down.

246
00:20:21,920 --> 00:20:22,400
Wait.

247
00:20:22,400 --> 00:20:26,960
We will not allow you to rescue a descendant of criminals.

248
00:20:29,120 --> 00:20:30,200
That's Klaus.

249
00:20:30,820 --> 00:20:32,840
And that chubby guy from the Golden Dawn.

250
00:20:34,420 --> 00:20:36,320
Seriously? You guys too?

251
00:20:36,840 --> 00:20:37,700
This sucks.

252
00:20:38,500 --> 00:20:40,580
So the others are acting the same way?

253
00:20:41,720 --> 00:20:42,600
Oh no!

254
00:20:42,600 --> 00:20:45,400
Cut it out!

255
00:20:45,780 --> 00:20:47,320
I don't want to fight my friends!

256
00:20:47,560 --> 00:20:48,440
Just wake up!

257
00:20:49,960 --> 00:20:51,320
Why are you...

258
00:20:51,320 --> 00:21:00,080
What?

259
00:21:00,560 --> 00:21:01,120
No.

260
00:21:01,120 --> 00:21:01,200
